questions.problem_statement:
Task: This program should print 1 + 2 + ... + n for each number n, using a recursive function:

def rec_sum(n):
if n == 1:
return 1
return n + rec_sum(n - 1)

q = int(input())
for _ in range(q):
print(rec_sum(int(input())))

It works for 5, but for 0 or -3 the calls never reach n == 1. They keep counting down until Python stops with RecursionError.

Fix the program:
• For n <= 0 the sum is empty, so rec_sum must return 0. Make this the base case, so the recursion always stops
• Keep rec_sum recursive (no loop and no formula)

Example: for the numbers 5, 0 and -3 the output is 15, 0 and 0.

questions.reference_solution:
def rec_sum(n):
    if n <= 0:              # was n == 1: missed 0 and negative numbers
        return 0
    return n + rec_sum(n - 1)


q = int(input())
for _ in range(q):
    print(rec_sum(int(input())))

text = input()
settings = {}

for part in text.split(";"):
    part = part.strip()
    if not part:
        continue
    try:
        key, value = part.split("=", 1)
    except ValueError:          # no "=" in this part: report it and skip only this part
        print(f"SKIPPED: {part}")
        continue

    key = key.strip()
    value = value.strip()
    try:
        settings[key] = int(value)
    except ValueError:          # not a number: keep the text
        settings[key] = value

if settings:
    for key, value in settings.items():
        kind = "int" if isinstance(value, int) else "str"
        print(f"{key}={value} ({kind})")
else:
    print("NO SETTINGS")

